# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/
*.obj
*.o
*.a
*.lib
*.ilk
compile_commands.json
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CTestTestfile.cmake
Testing/

# ── Release artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prebuilt binaries are attached to GitHub releases, not committed. `make`, CMake
# or scripts/build_windows.sh recreates them in seconds.
dist/
*.pdb
*.exe
*.dll
package/
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# ── Generated data and benchmark corpus ───────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/gen_data.py regenerates any of these byte-for-byte. A 1 GB CSV does not
# belong in a git object store. The harnesses that produce the numbers do ship:
# only the corpus they operate on is ignored.
data/
bench/*
!bench/*.py
!bench/*.sh
!bench/README.md
bench-results/
*.tessera.idx
*.csv.gz

# ── Vendored toolchains ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/build_windows.sh can use a Zig toolchain from tools/; it is downloaded,
# never committed (~400 MB unpacked).
tools/
.tools/
zig.tar.xz

# ── Local rendering scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/*.png are the screenshots that ship with the README; artifacts/ is where
# the snapshot tooling writes during development, including the inputs saved by
# tests/fuzz_tessera.py when a case fails.
artifacts/
fuzz-failure-*.csv
fuzz-mutation-*.csv
fuzz-hang-*.csv

# ── Generated package manifests ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A winget/Scoop manifest embeds the SHA-256 of the exact release artifact it
# installs, so these are generated from the published archives by
# scripts/gen_package_manifests.py and attached to the release. Committing them
# here would pin hashes of a different build. See packaging/README.md.
packaging/generated/

# ── Editor and OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
